      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The electron-spin resonance (ESR) was applied to examine human plasma and red cell lipids. In the lipids, the signal of ESR of alpha-tocopherylquinone was recorded. The concentration of the latter in the lipids was found to be elevated in coronary heart disease. Intramuscular injection of 30% oily solution of alpha-tocopherylquinone in a dose of 2 ml two times a day over three days entailed an increase in the concentration of alpha-tocopherylquinone in plasma and red cell lipids."},
